        {
          "id": 506503876,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This speeds up tests significantly on my Windows development VM. The results of running all tests and the decryption suite (which doesn't require extcap) are shown below.\n\n| Commit | Test | Time | Processes Spawned |\n| ---- | ---- | ---- | ---- |\n| 9ba1053237 (1 before 506f1c650f) | all | 379.479s | 885 |\n| 9ba1053237 (1 before 506f1c650f) | suite_decrypt | 59.882s | 100 |\n| c8246c9973 (current master) | all | 1134.810s | 6836 |\n| c8246c9973 (current master) | suite_decrypt | 199.149s | 1200 |\n| 4c73b3a1df (this MR) | all | 609.780s | 1413 |\n| 4c73b3a1df (this MR) | suite_decrypt | 84.847s | 111 |\n\nCommit 506f1c650f switched from calling extcap_register_preferences() conditionally to unconditionally. Process spawns were counted using Process Monitor with the filters \"Operation contains Process Create\" and \"Path contains run\\RelWithDebInfo\".",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
